Z||000000||The Fieromaster||10-08-2001||08:13 PM||||Sorry for the POOR image quality BUT my cam is a FLAMING POS that I got hella cheap!!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gauges1.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gauges2.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">       <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">    <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">               <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B>||||reg||1
Z||000001||kempo||10-08-2001||09:41 PM||||What are each of the pods for?  Looks good.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula||10-08-2001||10:00 PM||||where did you get them from?||||reg||1
Z||000003||The Fieromaster||10-09-2001||01:34 AM||||Well the pods hold the following... Boost/Vac, Air/fuel, and a Voltmeter (will be replaced with a Pyrometer as soon as i can afford one of the expensive things!)<BR>Yea yea I know its rice boyish to put in a boost gauge when my turbo wont go in till winter BUT they came out of my Eclipse GSX wich suffered an ill fated death!!  So I put them in, rather than buyin new ones (small chips in lenses and scratched paint) as a reminder of my Eclipse and what i WILL NOT let happen to my baby!<P>The gauge pod is from a Acura Integra! It is the FULL PILLER that i custom cut down and sanded smooth.  The top and bottom have a curved shape to how i sanded them to match the Fiero's interior scheme and lines!<P>--added--- Oh yea... The pods came from Summit Racing.  They also have 2 gauge pods that ARE NOT full pillars and I dont believe they need any cutting BUT as FieroJoe knows those are back ordered from now till hell freezes over (!?again?!).  Not to mention i needed 3 gauges anyway for when turbo is done (and that i know of no one else has a tri-pod... look im different... but we all knew that already  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> hehehe) <BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">        <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">     <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">                <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B><p>[This message has been edited by The Fieromaster (edited 10-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||10-09-2001||01:06 PM||||Yeah, Im not happy about waiting until the end of this month to put in my gauges!  Oh well, there isn't much I can do about it either.  I did find some paint that matches the color about right though, so it dosent have to be black.<P>You should try to put some red bulbs in there to make them light up to match the rest of the gauges, or maybe some other color.  That'd look cool.||||reg||1
Z||000005||West Coast Fiero||10-09-2001||01:30 PM||||I like the tri-pod, we did something similar for our turbo 3800....<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.cwestco.com/Interior/Gauge_box_gif/Gaugebox_w_gauge_500.jpg"> <P>also seen here at....  <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/Interior/gaugebox.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/Interior/gaugebox.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||The Fieromaster||10-09-2001||03:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR><B>I like the tri-pod, we did something similar for our turbo 3800....<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cwestco.com/Interior/Gauge_box_gif/Gaugebox_w_gauge_500.jpg">  <P>also seen here at....  <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/Interior/gaugebox.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/Interior/gaugebox.html</A> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wow looks good!!  I am doing somthing similar to that to hold my boost controler, remote ignition advance, turbo timer, and status lights (Scramble Armed/Fire,and warning lights for boost limits and any other warning lights i may wire in) I am gonna use a GT center pod to mount it all in so it has the stock look!  As for the face... dark tinted lexan so you cant see the letters of the warning lights until its lit up!!  Should be COOL! Althoug I need a GT center pod though!!<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">       <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">    <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">               <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B>||||reg||1
